{"body":"## What to build\n\nLet a Pi assistant create an isolated research cycle, accumulate a research plan, inspect it, survive restart, and deliberately resume or archive it without losing its history. No paid execution is initiated by planning or resume.\n\nSource: [PRD-010: Integrated Research Cycle](https://github.com/feniix/pi-extensions/blob/main/docs/prd/PRD-010-pi-exa-integrated-research-cycle.md) (v1.1).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Planning tools expose cycle identity, revision, criteria, selected evidence, assumptions, gaps, and lifecycle status through step/status/summary.\n- [ ] Curated state is stored in user-local storage outside git, with schema versioning and atomic writes; credentials, raw planning chatter, and full exploratory response archives are excluded.\n- [ ] Restart never automatically attaches the latest plan; explicit resume transfers exclusive ownership and prevents simultaneous execution ownership across sessions.\n- [ ] Separate sessions/projects do not share active state or budget authorization; resuming a known saved cycle is deliberate.\n- [ ] Reset detaches and archives without deleting ledger/attempt records, clearing unknown outcomes, authorizing new spending, or cancelling remote work. Existing outstanding/unknown records produce a warning.\n- [ ] Archived records remain inspectable; completed records cannot become executable by reset/resume. No destructive cycle deletion is introduced.\n- [ ] Test-first lifecycle, restart, isolation, ownership, and write-failure tests pass. Existing standalone Pi and MCP behavior remains unchanged, with incomplete integrated execution gated.\n\nWrite or update failing tests first for behavioral changes. Each slice must remain independently verifiable; incomplete integrated behavior stays gated and existing behavior remains supported.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #152 — Verify feasibility and settle the execution contract\n","comments":[],"title":"pi-exa: Create, persist, resume, and archive isolated research cycles","url":"https://github.com/feniix/pi-extensions/issues/153"}

