{"body":"## What to build

Let the assistant build and preview the exact structured research artifact that an integrated Agent submission will use, with conflicts surfaced before spending.

Source: [PRD-010: Integrated Research Cycle](https://github.com/feniix/pi-extensions/blob/main/docs/prd/PRD-010-pi-exa-integrated-research-cycle.md) (v1.1).

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Planner updates support research goals, scope, constraints, criteria, labeled assumptions, gaps, selected evidence, optional processing/exclusion records, structured output contract, execution controls, and an explicit optional continuation reference.
- [ ] Summary compiles a versioned artifact tied to cycle identity and plan revision; input/exclusion rows remain distinct from selected source evidence.
- [ ] Preview and eventual submission share the same compiler and artifact representation. Raw planning chatter and unselected candidates are excluded.
- [ ] Structured conflicts produce actionable errors; compatible additions use the agreed merge rules. Stale artifact references cannot silently execute a changed plan.
- [ ] Preview is optional, and operator approval of every brief is not required. Compilation does not perform paid calls.
- [ ] Test-first artifact/schema, conflict, revision, provenance, and row/evidence separation checks pass; standalone text/object research modes and MCP contracts remain unchanged.

Write or update failing tests first for behavioral changes. Each slice must remain independently verifiable; incomplete integrated behavior stays gated and existing behavior remains supported.

## Blocked by

- #153 — Create, persist, resume, and archive isolated research cycles
