{"body":"## What to build

Let the assistant perform explicitly cycle-attributed exploratory Exa calls under an approved best-effort total budget, with meaningful pre-call assessment and auditable usage afterward.

Source: [PRD-010: Integrated Research Cycle](https://github.com/feniix/pi-extensions/blob/main/docs/prd/PRD-010-pi-exa-integrated-research-cycle.md) (v1.1).

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Use the agreed operator-authorization representation to record a cycle budget and scoped amendments/exceptions; do not treat an assistant-provided number alone as proof of consent.
- [ ] Every attributable paid exploratory Exa call assesses confirmed spend, unresolved/unknown liabilities, outstanding calls, and proposed-call estimates before dispatch.
- [ ] Autonomous dispatch requires a defensible combined estimate within permission. Insufficient balance or unbounded uncertainty returns an actionable approval requirement without dispatch; unknown cost is never zero by default.
- [ ] Concurrent calls atomically share pending assessments rather than each consuming the same balance; estimates record their basis.
- [ ] Actual usage reconciles pending estimates without double-counting, preserves unknown costs where reporting is unavailable, and reports overspend before further paid work. Other providers costs remain outside the Exa ledger.
- [ ] Ledger and permission state survive restart/archive; reset does not authorize another research cycle.
- [ ] Test-first approval, concurrency, timeout/unknown-cost, reconciliation, and overspend scenarios pass. No live spending occurs without permission; unrelated standalone calls and MCP remain unchanged.

Write or update failing tests first for behavioral changes. Each slice must remain independently verifiable; incomplete integrated behavior stays gated and existing behavior remains supported.

## Blocked by

- #153 — Create, persist, resume, and archive isolated research cycles
